 74-W- 182 ORNL Resonance Evaluation Including Covariance         7431 1451
 (ORNL AUG 2014)                                                  7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
 L. Leal, M. Pigni, K. Guber, D. Wiarda, and G. Arbanas           7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
 W-182 resolved resonance parameter evaluation was done in the    7431 1451
energy range form 1e-5 eV to 10 keV with the SAMMY code[ref1].    7431 1451
Capture and transmission measurements for enriched W-182 and      7431 1451
natural tungsten were used in the evaluation. The measurements    7431 1451
were done at the Oak Ridge Linear Accelerator (ORELA)[ref2] and   7431 1451
at the Geel Linear Accelerator (GELINA), Belgium[ref3]. Neutron   7431 1451
transmission and capture data were measured in the energy range   7431 1451
from 20 eV to 10 keV.                                             7431 1451
 Thermal cross section[ref4] data available in the EXFOR library  7431 1451
were also used in the evaluation.                                 7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
 Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also obtained in    7431 1451
the SAMMY evaluation process in the energy region 1e-5 eV-10 keV. 7431 1451
The RML formalist (LRF=7) was used for the resonance parameters   7431 1451
and the compact formalism (LCOMP=2) for the covariance matrix.    7431 1451
  Thermal cross section and uncertainty calculated with SAMMY and 7431 1451
the PUFF codes are compared with the values listed in the ATLAS   7431 1451
of Neutron Resoances in the table below. Also shown is the        7431 1451
capture resonance integral, Coherent scattering length and the    7431 1451
effective radius R'.                                              7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
    Cross Section        ORNL (b)           Atlas (b)             7431 1451
    -------------        --------           ---------             7431 1451
       Total         29.18 +/- 0.40             -                 7431 1451
       Capt          20.31 +/- 0.64        19.90 +/-  0.30        7431 1451
       Scat           8.87 +/- 0.28         8.84 +/-  0.30        7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
 Capture Res. Int.  618.41 +/- 0.17       600.00 +/- 60.0         7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
        R'            7.64 fm               8.3  +/-  0.2  fm     7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
        b_coher       7.11 fm              7.04  +/-  0.04 fm     7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
 Average cross section and related uncertainties calculated in    7431 1451
energy group 0.0253 eV - 0.3 eV are listed in the table below.    7431 1451
                                                                  7431 1451
